    <node id="Basal cell skin cancer">
      <data key="d0">Basal cell skin cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of skin cancer, also known as basal cell carcinoma (BCC), which is the most common type of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin">
      <data key="d0">Skin</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The largest organ of the human body, which serves as a barrier against bacteria and chemicals and helps control body temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;The largest organ of the body that protects against invaders, controls body temperature, and allows sensations of touch, heat, and cold.&lt;SEP&gt;The outer layer of the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;The outermost layer of the human body covering the surface of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Epidermis">
      <data key="d0">Epidermis</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The top layer of the skin, which provides a waterproof barrier and creates skin color.&lt;SEP&gt;The outermost layer of the skin that provides a waterproof barrier and creates skin color.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dermis">
      <data key="d0">Dermis</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The middle layer of the skin, which includes connective tissue, blood vessels, oil and sweat glands, nerves, and hair follicles.&lt;SEP&gt;The middle layer of the skin containing connective tissue, hair follicles, and sweat glands.&lt;SEP&gt;The layer beneath the epidermis in the skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hypodermis">
      <data key="d0">Hypodermis</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The deepest layer of the skin, which is made up of fat and connective tissue.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Squamous cells">
      <data key="d0">Squamous cells</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Flat cells found in the upper part of the epidermis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells found in the tissues that form the surface of the skin and in other areas of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basal cells">
      <data key="d0">Basal cells</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Cells found in the lower part of the epidermis that constantly divide to form new cells that replace the squamous cells on the skin's surface.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Melanocytes">
      <data key="d0">Melanocytes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Cells located in the lower part of the epidermis that produce melanin, responsible for hair, skin, and eye color and protect the skin from harmful UV rays.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UV radiation">
      <data key="d0">UV radiation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation from the sun or other sources like tanning beds that can harm the DNA inside basal skin cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin cancer">
      <data key="d0">Skin cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of cancer that forms in the cells of the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that develops in the skin cells, characterized by uncontrolled cell growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788521994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgery is a broad term encompassing various medical procedures aimed at removing or repairing damaged or diseased tissue, organs, or conditions. It can involve the removal of cancerous tissue, such as in the case of squamous cell skin cancer, which may include methods like curettage and electrodesiccation, PDEMA/Mohs surgery, and standard surgical excision. Additionally, surgery can be used to treat or remove a disease or condition, often involving the removal of tumors or diseased tissue. In some instances, it may also involve the repair of damaged tissue or organs, such as in cases of bladder cancer where the entire bladder might need to be removed. Overall, surgery represents a critical component of medical treatment, focusing on the removal or repair of problematic tissue or organs to restore health and function.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-154&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522000</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiation therapy">
      <data key="d0">Radiation therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation therapy is a form of cancer treatment that utilizes high-energy radiation to target and eliminate cancer cells. This method is particularly effective for squamous cell skin cancer, where it is often employed post-surgery to destroy any remaining cancerous tissue. Radiation therapy is also a common approach for treating various types of cancer, including advanced-stage prostate cancer, where it helps in killing cancer cells and shrinking tumors. Additionally, it is used in the treatment of anal cancer, though this application may come with side effects such as potential infertility due to damage to the ovaries and disruption of hormone production necessary for natural pregnancy. Overall, radiation therapy represents a versatile and powerful tool in the arsenal against cancer, offering hope to patients through its ability to harness the power of high-energy radiation to combat disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522005</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic therapy">
      <data key="d0">Systemic therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic therapy refers to a broad category of cancer treatments that involve the use of drugs to target and kill cancer cells throughout the body. This approach can include various methods such as chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy, depending on the specific type of cancer being treated. For instance, systemic therapy is commonly employed in the treatment of squamous cell skin cancer, where it may be combined with other therapies like surgery or radiation. The term "systemic therapy" encompasses a range of treatment approaches aimed at eradicating cancer cells systemically, making it a crucial component in the management of many types of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="basal cell skin cancer">
      <data key="d0">basal cell skin cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of skin cancer characterized by the recurrence of cancer in the area where it was originally found or its spread to other parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="adrenal glands">
      <data key="d0">adrenal glands</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Small, yellow glands located on top of each kidney, producing hormones that regulate various bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="adrenal tumors">
      <data key="d0">adrenal tumors</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumors that form in the adrenal glands, which can be benign or malignant, affecting hormone production and causing various symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="adrenocortical carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">adrenocortical carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A rare type of adrenal gland cancer that begins in the adrenal cortex, producing more than one hormone.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="aldosteronoma">
      <data key="d0">aldosteronoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A benign adrenal tumor that produces excessive aldosterone, causing hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cushing syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Cushing syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A condition caused by excessive cortisol production, typically due to an adrenal tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neuroblastoma">
      <data key="d0">Neuroblastoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A rare type of cancer that affects children aged 5 and under, often found in infants, and can spread to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare type of adrenal tumor that is cancerous and affects children ages 5 and under.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adrenal gland cancer">
      <data key="d0">Adrenal gland cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A rare cancer that starts in one or both of the adrenal glands.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adrenocortical carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Adrenocortical carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An adrenal cancer that starts in the adrenal cortex.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pheochromocytoma">
      <data key="d0">Pheochromocytoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tumor that begins in the adrenal medulla and is characterized by symptoms of high blood pressure, headache, rapid heartbeat, and sweating.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adenoma">
      <data key="d0">Adenoma</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">The most common type of adrenal gland tumor, also referred to as adrenocortical adenoma, which is a noncancerous tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;The most common type of polyp, which can become invasive rectal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of polyp that can become invasive colon cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of polyp that can develop into invasive colon cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-059&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-121&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that can put one at risk for developing an adrenal tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carney complex">
      <data key="d0">Carney complex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that can put one at risk for developing an adrenal tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP)">
      <data key="d0">Familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that can put one at risk for developing an adrenal tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare inherited cancer syndrome causing hundreds to thousands of polyps in the colon and rectum.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-059</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hereditary paragangliomapheochromocytoma (PGL/PCC) syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Hereditary paragangliomapheochromocytoma (PGL/PCC) syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that can put one at risk for developing an adrenal tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Li-Fraumeni syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Li-Fraumeni syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that can put one at risk for developing an adrenal tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;A genetic condition associated with an increased risk of various cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-078</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522009</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NCCN Guidelines for Patients">
      <data key="d0">NCCN Guidelines for Patients</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The NCCN Guidelines for Patients are a comprehensive set of recommendations designed to assist patients with cancer in understanding their care options and making informed decisions about their treatment. These guidelines, developed by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, cover various aspects of cancer care, including specific conditions such as acute myeloid leukemia (AML). They are available online at NCCN.org/patientguidelines and through the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app. The guidelines are based on the NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology, which are expert-recommended and clearly explained to help patients and caregivers navigate the complexities of cancer care. These resources aim to provide clear and up-to-date information on cancer care, treatment options, and managing side effects and distress during cancer care.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-068&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-077&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-118&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-154&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-168&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-169</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
