    <node id="Lynch syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Lynch syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lynch syndrome, also known as hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer (HNPCC), is a genetic condition characterized by an increased risk of developing various types of cancer. This inherited cancer syndrome is caused by mutations in the mismatch repair genes, primarily MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, and PMS2. Individuals with Lynch syndrome have a higher predisposition to developing colorectal, endometrial, ovarian, and other cancers, such as bladder cancer. It is estimated that about 5-10% of all colorectal cancers and up to 20% of ovarian cancers are due to Lynch syndrome. The condition is hereditary, meaning it can be passed down through generations, and it significantly raises the risk of developing multiple types of cancer throughout a person's lifetime.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-059&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-078&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
