    <node id="Squamous cell skin cancer">
      <data key="d0">Squamous cell skin cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of skin cancer that is the second most common type of skin cancer, highly treatable, and can often be cured.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of skin cancer characterized by abnormal growth of squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that affects the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of skin cancer characterized by the abnormal growth of squamous cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522021</data>
