    <node id="Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer is a broad term encompassing a diverse group of diseases characterized by uncontrolled cell growth and division. This uncontrolled growth leads to the formation of tumors and can result in the abnormal cell growth spreading to other parts of the body, potentially invading and damaging nearby tissues. Cancer is often described as a disease where the normal regulatory mechanisms that control cell growth and division fail, allowing cells to multiply uncontrollably. This process can lead to the development of tumors, which may grow large enough to cause symptoms or interfere with bodily functions. The term cancer is used to describe various types of diseases, including but not limited to, breast cancer, lung cancer, and skin cancer, among others.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-107&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-108&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-136&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-152&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
