    <node id="Targeted therapy">
      <data key="d0">Targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Targeted therapy is a form of systemic cancer treatment that specifically targets and attacks various receptors, molecules, or pathways involved in the growth and survival of cancer cells. This approach focuses on unique features of cancer cells, aiming to disrupt the mechanisms that enable cancer growth and proliferation. Targeted therapies can be categorized under systemic treatments, which means they affect the entire body rather than just localized areas. These therapies are designed to be more precise and less toxic compared to traditional chemotherapy, as they aim to target specific molecules or pathways that are essential for cancer cell survival but not present in normal cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522058</data>
