    <node id="Immunotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Immunotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunotherapy is a type of systemic therapy that utilizes the patient's immune system to fight cancer. It involves boosting the body's natural defenses against cancer cells by enhancing the immune system's ability to identify and eliminate cancerous tissues. This approach can be particularly effective in treating advanced-stage cancers, such as prostate cancer, where traditional treatments may have limited success. Immunotherapy works by stimulating the immune system to recognize and attack cancer cells, thereby improving the body's ability to find and destroy cancerous cells. It is considered a promising treatment option for various types of cancer, leveraging the body's own defense mechanisms to combat disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-125&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194</data>
