    <node id="Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor refers to a physical mass of abnormal tissue that can grow in various ways, including in an uncontrolled manner, an unusual pattern, or an unusual manner. These masses can be benign or malignant, depending on the nature of the abnormal cell growth. A tumor is characterized by the abnormal growth of cells, leading to the formation of a mass that can develop in different parts of the body. The term "tumor" encompasses a broad range of conditions where abnormal tissue growth occurs, often resulting from genetic mutations or other factors. The primary tumor, also known as the main tumor, is the initial site of tumor development, which may later spread to other parts of the body through a process called metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-107&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-158&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-159&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-166&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-167</data>
