    </node>
    <node id="Lung">
      <data key="d0">Lung</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">An organ in the chest cavity that is part of the respiratory system.&lt;SEP&gt;A pair of organs involved in respiration, delivering oxygen to the blood and removing carbon dioxide.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ in the chest cavity that is responsible for breathing and gas exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ in the respiratory system responsible for gas exchange.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522076</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone marrow">
      <data key="d0">Bone marrow</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Bone marrow is a spongy tissue found in the center of most bones, where blood cells are produced. It is characterized as a sponge-like structure that plays a crucial role in hematopoiesis, the process of blood cell formation. This tissue is essential for the development and production of various types of blood cells, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. Bone marrow is also involved in the maturation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are precursors to all blood cells. The presence of lymphoblasts in acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) can affect bone marrow function, leading to reduced blood cell production. Additionally, bone marrow contains numerous blood vessels that facilitate the transport of nutrients and oxygen necessary for the growth and maintenance of blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-068&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-153&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adenocarcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Adenocarcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of non-small cell lung cancer formed from cells that line the alveoli.&lt;SEP&gt;A subtype of non-small cell lung cancer characterized by the presence of glandular structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that forms in an adenoma, the most common type of rectal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that arises from glandular tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancers that form in glandular cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cervical cancer characterized by the presence of glandular cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-059&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-133&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-141</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522082</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large cell carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Large cell carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of non-small cell lung cancer formed from large cells in the airways.&lt;SEP&gt;A subtype of non-small cell lung cancer characterized by the presence of large, undifferentiated cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019</data>
