    <node id="Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC)">
      <data key="d0">Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of cancer that starts in the thin, flat cells found in the inner lining of the esophagus.&lt;SEP&gt;The most common type of mouth cancer, characterized by the presence of squamous cells that form the surface lining of the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The most common type of mouth cancer, forming in the thin, flat cells of the mucous membranes of the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The most common type of nasopharyngeal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The most common type of nasopharyngeal cancer, forming in the thin, flat cells of the mucus membranes of the nasopharynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127</data>
