    </node>
    <node id="Liver">
      <data key="d0">Liver</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The liver is a large organ situated in the upper right part of the abdomen, playing a crucial role in metabolism, detoxification, and storage of nutrients. It is involved in various metabolic processes, including the production of bile and the processing of chemicals. The liver also filters blood, makes bile, and produces lymph, contributing to its multifaceted functions in the human body. As the largest organ in the human body, it processes nutrients, detoxifies harmful substances, and produces bile, making it essential for maintaining overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-159&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-162&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-163&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192</data>
