      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Soft, spongy tissue in the center of most bones where new blood cells are made.&lt;SEP&gt;A spongy tissue inside bones that produces blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A spongy tissue found in bones that produces blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The soft, spongy tissue inside bones where blood cells are produced.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-168</data>
