    <node id="Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL)">
      <data key="d0">Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL)</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of lymphomas that develop from B lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer that develops from lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer of lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522091</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="lymph nodes">
      <data key="d0">lymph nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymph nodes are small, bean-shaped structures throughout the body that play a crucial role in the immune system. They filter lymph fluid and help in catching and filtering out foreign particles, harmful cells, and even cancer cells. Lymph nodes are also known to produce white blood cells and fight infections. These organs are essential components of the immune system, working together to maintain the body's health by identifying and neutralizing potential threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-187&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522094</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
