    </node>
    <node id="Immunophenotyping">
      <data key="d0">Immunophenotyping</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method used to identify the type of lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;A process used to identify markers on cells, particularly in the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that uses antibodies to detect the presence or absence of white blood cell antigens called biomarkers.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that uses antibodies to detect the presence or absence of white blood cell antigens.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-070</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522094</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d0">Lymphocytes</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that play a crucial role in the immune system by fighting infections and preventing diseases. Found in blood and lymph tissue, as well as all organs in the body, lymphocytes help combat and neutralize pathogens. They are involved in various aspects of the immune response, including the production of antibodies and the activation of other immune cells. Additionally, some lymphocytes can transform into lymphoblasts during the development of acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL). These cells are essential for maintaining overall health and protecting the body against a wide range of pathogens.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522098</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Biopsy is a medical procedure used to obtain tissue samples for examination. It involves the removal of a small piece of tissue or fluid from the body for analysis by a pathologist. This process aids in diagnosing various conditions, including cancer, by examining the tissue samples under a microscope. Biopsies can be performed on different parts of the body, such as the prostate, pancreas, and other areas, depending on the suspected condition. The procedure is often used to determine the presence of cancer or to stage the disease accurately. Biopsies may also involve the removal of a sample of cells, fluid, or tissue for testing, and they can be conducted using various tools, including those attached to endoscopic instruments like cystoscopes. Overall, biopsies play a crucial role in medical diagnostics by providing critical information for accurate diagnosis and treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-095&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-103&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-117&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-156&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-161&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-163&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-166&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-170&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-186&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
