      <data key="d0">MRI scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MRI scan, also known as Magnetic Resonance Imaging, is a diagnostic imaging technique that uses radio waves and powerful magnets to create detailed images of the body. This non-invasive procedure allows healthcare professionals to visualize internal structures without the use of radiation, making it particularly useful for examining soft tissues such as the brain, muscles, and organs. MRI scans provide high-resolution images that can help diagnose various medical conditions, including tumors, infections, and injuries. The process involves lying on a table that slides into a large, tube-shaped machine, which generates strong magnetic fields and radio waves to capture detailed cross-sectional images of the body. These images are then analyzed by radiologists to identify any abnormalities or diseases. MRI scans are widely used in clinical settings due to their accuracy and ability to differentiate between different types of tissue, offering valuable insights for patient care and treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-166</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522114</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagnostic imaging technique using high-energy sound waves.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic imaging technique that uses sound waves to create images of internal organs and tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic imaging technique used to guide a lymph node biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging technique used to visualize internal structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146</data>
