    <node id="PET scan">
      <data key="d0">PET scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">PET scan, also known as positron emission tomography, is a diagnostic imaging technique used in medicine to detect cancer cells. It involves the use of a radioactive drug, often referred to as a tracer, which is injected into the patient's body. This tracer accumulates in areas of high metabolic activity, such as cancerous cells, allowing doctors to visualize and locate these cells within the body. PET scans can provide valuable information about the presence, location, and extent of cancer, as well as the effectiveness of treatment. The process typically begins with the administration of a radioactive sugar-based substance or other tracer, which is then detected by specialized cameras that capture images of the body. These images help healthcare professionals make informed decisions regarding diagnosis and treatment plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-103&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522119</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="pathologist">
      <data key="d0">pathologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical doctor specializing in the examination of tissues and fluids to diagnose diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who examines tissue samples under a microscope to identify the presence of disease.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who specializes in the examination of tissues and fluids to determine the presence of disease.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical specialist who examines tissues and bodily fluids to diagnose diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor specializing in evaluating cells and tissues to diagnose disease.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who specializes in the study of tissues and organs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-114&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-134&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180</data>
