    <node id="Next-generation sequencing (NGS)">
      <data key="d0">Next-generation sequencing (NGS)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method used to determine a portion of a person’s DNA sequence to show if a gene has any mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to determine a portion of a person’s DNA sequence, showing mutations that might affect gene function.&lt;SEP&gt;A method for determining a portion of a person’s DNA sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-throughput method used to determine the DNA sequence or gene changes of cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to determine a portion of a person’s DNA sequence.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
