    <node id="Polymerase chain reaction (PCR)">
      <data key="d0">Polymerase chain reaction (PCR)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method used to amplify a specific segment of DNA in vitro.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that can make millions or billions of copies of DNA or RNA, useful for NGS and detecting abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;A lab process that makes millions or billions of copies of DNA.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that can make millions or billions of copies of DNA or RNA.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
