    <node id="Blood">
      <data key="d0">Blood</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood is a critical component of the circulatory system, responsible for transporting essential substances throughout the body. It is primarily composed of plasma, which serves as the liquid medium, and cellular elements including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. Red blood cells, also known as erythrocytes, are responsible for carrying oxygen to tissues and removing carbon dioxide. White blood cells, or leukocytes, play a crucial role in the immune system by fighting off infections and diseases. Platelets, or thrombocytes, help in the clotting process to prevent excessive bleeding. Blood also contains various proteins and other substances necessary for maintaining homeostasis and supporting various physiological processes. As a fluid that circulates throughout the body, blood carries oxygen, nutrients, and waste products to and from the cells, ensuring the proper functioning of all bodily systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-068&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173</data>
