    <node id="Ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Ultrasound is a diagnostic imaging technique that uses high-energy sound waves to create images of internal body structures. This medical imaging method involves the use of high-frequency sound waves to produce detailed images of internal organs and structures, allowing healthcare professionals to visualize and analyze the condition of various parts of the body non-invasively. Ultrasound is often employed in clinical settings to diagnose and monitor conditions such as pregnancy, heart function, and abnormalities in organs like the liver, kidneys, and thyroid gland. It is a versatile tool used across different medical fields, providing valuable insights into the health of patients through the creation of real-time images of internal tissues and organs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-103&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-116&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038</data>
