    </node>
    <node id="Microsatellite instability (MSI)">
      <data key="d0">Microsatellite instability (MSI)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic alteration where the number of repeats in microsatellite sequences varies significantly compared to normal, often associated with certain types of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where cancer cells have more than a normal number of microsatellites, often due to defective mismatch repair (dMMR) genes.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where cancer cells have more than a normal number of microsatellites.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where cancer cells have DNA mutations preventing errors from being fixed.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522134</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor mutational burden (TMB)">
      <data key="d0">Tumor mutational burden (TMB)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The total number of mutations found in a tumor, which can be used to guide treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The number of mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522134</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
