      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagnostic imaging technique that uses X-rays to create detailed cross-sectional images of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of imaging test that uses X-rays to create detailed cross-sectional images of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of imaging technique used to visualize internal structures of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;CT stands for Computed Tomography, a medical imaging technique that uses X-rays to produce detailed cross-sectional images of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed tomography scan used to visualize internal structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical imaging technique that uses x-rays to create detailed images of the body from different angles.</data>
