      <data key="d0">Prostate-specific antigen (PSA)</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A protein made by the prostate gland that nourishes and helps transmit semen.&lt;SEP&gt;A protein made inside the prostate gland, used as a marker for potential prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of the amount of PSA in the bloodstream, used to assess the risk of prostate cancer.</data>
