    <node id="Grade">
      <data key="d0">Grade</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A measure of the abnormality of tumor cells under a microscope, used to determine the aggressiveness of the cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification system used to describe the appearance of tumor cells under a microscope, which helps determine the aggressiveness and potential for recurrence of the cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure used in cancer staging to describe the abnormality of tumor cells under a microscope, influencing the growth and spread rate of the cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A rating of how abnormal the cells of a glioma are, used to predict the growth rate and prognosis of the tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;An estimate of the rate that the cancer is growing, categorized as low grade (slow) or high grade (fast).</data>
