    <node id="Stage I">
      <data key="d0">Stage I</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The first stage of cancer, indicating a smaller tumor size.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in the classification of anal cancer where the tumor is 2 cm or smaller and has not spread to nearby lymph nodes or to areas far from the anus.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer that has not spread beyond the pelvis.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer based on its size and how far it has spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522138</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage II">
      <data key="d0">Stage II</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The second stage of cancer, indicating a slightly larger tumor size.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in the classification of anal cancer where the tumor is larger than 2 cm but not larger than 5 cm or larger than 5 cm and has not spread to nearby lymph nodes or to areas far from the anus.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer that has not spread beyond the pelvis.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer based on its size and how far it has spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788522138</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage III">
      <data key="d0">Stage III</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The third stage of cancer, indicating a larger tumor size.&lt;SEP&gt;A stage in the classification of anal cancer where there may be cancer in nearby lymph nodes. Substages include T1, N1, M0 or T2, N1, M, T4, N0, M, and T3, N1, M0 or T4, N1, M.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer that has not spread beyond the pelvis.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of cancer based on its size and how far it has spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191</data>
