    <node id="Pelvis">
      <data key="d0">Pelvis</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The pelvis is a complex anatomical structure that serves as a crucial component of the human body, particularly in the lower abdomen. It is composed of several bones, including the sacrum, the two hipbones, and the coccyx, which together form a basin-shaped structure. This structure plays a vital role in supporting the spinal column and protecting the abdominal organs, such as the intestines, bladder, and reproductive organs. The pelvis is also involved in various functions, including childbirth, locomotion, and maintaining balance. Its location is defined by its position between the hip bones, extending from the lower part of the spine down to the pelvic inlet, which marks the boundary between the pelvic cavity and the abdominal cavity. The pelvis is essential for the support and protection of the lower body structures and contributes significantly to the overall stability and functionality of the human anatomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-158&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-159&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
